cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DESQ: Dynamic Ensemble Selection for Quantitative Stock Selection"
message: "If you use this software or the reviewer reproducibility kit, please cite the specific release DOI (see below) rather than the head of the main branch."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Tung-Li"
    family-names: "Chen"
    affiliation: "National Taiwan University"
    # Add ORCID once available; changes are non-breaking for the DOI record.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tunglich/DESQ"
license: MIT
version: "1.0-desq"
date-released: "2026-08-03"
# The DOI below is minted automatically by Zenodo when the v1.0-desq release
# is published on GitHub. Replace <TO_BE_ASSIGNED_BY_ZENODO> with the string
# Zenodo prints (e.g. "10.5281/zenodo.1234567") in the follow-up commit; the
# release itself is immutable so the citation remains valid.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "<TO_BE_ASSIGNED_BY_ZENODO>"
    description: "Concept + version DOI for the v1.0-desq reviewer snapshot."
keywords:
  - dynamic-ensemble-selection
  - deslib
  - quantitative-finance
  - reproducible-research
  - stock-selection
  - tw50
abstract: >-
  DESQ is the reference implementation of the DES-based quantitative
  stock-selection pipeline used in the IEEE Access submission.
  The v1.0-desq release ships a full reviewer reproducibility kit:
  SHA-256 fingerprints of the shipped Taiwan-50 features, a yfinance
  cross-check for the 2330 canary prices, a 3-stage smoke pipeline, and
  a GitHub Actions workflow that re-runs the falsifiable checks on every
  push (see reproducibility/README.md).
